#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124194 :question/id #uuid "a2c947c7-9873-5137-91ca-4fe0b42e9bb7" :question/math-academy-id "e-11021" :question/problem "Find the domain of the function $z = \\dfrac {\\sqrt {y+1}}{x+y}.$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n{\\left\\{  \\begin{array}{l}y + 1 \\ge  0 \\\\ x + y \\ne  0\\end{array} \\right. }\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n{\\left\\{  \\begin{array}{l}y \\ge  - 1 \\\\ y \\ne  - x\\end{array} \\right. }\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\big\\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, y \\geq -1, \\: y \\neq -x \\big\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124195 :question/id #uuid "42cbeba7-685e-5782-9695-9671d16b7f80" :question/math-academy-id "e-11022" :question/problem "Sketch the domain of $g(x,y)=\\dfrac{1}{\\ln(x+y)}.$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n{\\left\\{  \\begin{array}{l}x + y > 0 \\\\ \\ln   ( x + y ) \\ne  0\\end{array} \\right. }\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n{\\left\\{  \\begin{array}{l}x + y > 0 \\\\ x + y \\ne  1\\end{array} \\right. }\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n{\\left\\{  \\begin{array}{l}y > - x \\\\ y \\ne  1 - x\\end{array} \\right. }\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD = \\left \\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\, : \\, y \\gt -x, \\, y \\neq 1-x \\right \\}.\n$$\n\nNow, we plot the corresponding domain. \n\n- Starting with $y> -x,$ we draw a dashed line $y=-x$ and shade the region *above* the line.\n\n- Then, we draw a dashed line $y=1-x$ through the shaded region.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](images/6a/6aa1aaeadb177cf5a80bcb12a247725cb3396586e7516c3ba30b46b03a9d2612.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124196 :question/id #uuid "59fa0287-0562-5cf2-8469-946a69dc8adf" :question/math-academy-id "e-11025" :question/problem "The function $f(x,y)$ is defined as \n\n$$\nf(x,y) = y^2 - \\log_3(x - 7).\n$$\n\nEvaluate this function at the point $(10,3).$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(10,3),$ we substitute $x = 10$ and $y = 3$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(10,3) & =({y}^{2}-{log}_{3}⁡(x-7)){|}_{(10,3)} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}-{log}_{3}⁡(10-7) \\\\  & =9-{log}_{3}⁡(3) \\\\  & =9-1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(10,3)=8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124198 :question/id #uuid "bdae9fe0-a491-531b-ac36-7a37d2c32f16" :question/math-academy-id "e-11029" :question/problem "Find the domain of the function $z= \\dfrac{\\ln (2x+y)}{\\sqrt{x}}.$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive,\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities: \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y>0 \\\\ x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\big\\{(x, y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, 2x+y >0, \\: x > 0 \\big\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124796 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "830e64ce-d2c2-545c-953f-86fe6ab92ffe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: x^{2} + y^{2} \\le 9, x + y = 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121374} {:answer/id #uuid "93b44adb-3bf5-5139-9e68-748d2d7726ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The domain is the entire $xy$-plane" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121375} {:answer/id #uuid "01d329a2-ba09-5bd8-b49b-e49d1075ba9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: x^{2} + y^{2} \\le 9, x + y \\ne 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121376} {:answer/id #uuid "53d3a6b8-4585-5831-b9ed-578fb69f99d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: x^{2} + y^{2} > 9, x + y = 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121377} {:answer/id #uuid "7dd3c355-758b-5568-9b07-935bffe69eb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: x^{2} + y^{2} = 9, x + y \\ne 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121378}] :answer-field/id #uuid "7afdfc8b-8829-5a20-b515-92d1bb9cac1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121373}] :question/id #uuid "162e30d5-d50f-5735-b877-da5a3c0fc4f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-158177" :question/problem "Find the domain of the function $z = \\frac{\\sqrt{9 - x^{2} - y^{2}}}{x + y}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124797 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10308432-7ae2-570a-9b7d-c6dde8008165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x+y>0,\\,y\\ne 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272532} {:answer/id #uuid "4a33180e-a04c-5a49-800b-504ef37a4c7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x+y>0,\\,y>0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273017} {:answer/id #uuid "5a1b111d-c8c4-5131-ad00-17b4845eb7b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x+y\\ge 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273159} {:answer/id #uuid "b23ffefe-40d9-5a