domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0\\,⟹\\,{y}^{2}<{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,-|x|<y<|x|\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-|x|<y<|x|}.\n$$\n\nSince the inequality involves the $<$ sign, the curves are *not* part of the domain. Therefore, we draw the dashed lines $y=-|x|$ and $y=|x|,$ and shade the area *below* the curve $y=|x|,$ and *above* the curve $y=-|x|.$\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](images/c0/c06082999e1737b6e4ea5d32a3d8d77a271e3db49c38cc3725422bcb979676d0.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275455 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12a032bb-0889-591e-85b8-47a69d4ec2f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b8/b8fe923f727ca57a8a2cfc756b93c0ed522bdd9edcc06c8097bead979c8e4b15.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272553} {:answer/id #uuid "254a9485-1846-5deb-bc9e-aceea2bd5ccd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/09/09a061a81ca4b3201e9b97ad15354c14003e41d610c2892f5b6ba468761e83b7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272714} {:answer/id #uuid "36debd9c-b9be-5cca-b475-3c4b38be0a0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/39/39360eae2b0e74a944c4e5c40e5677460c10b3259824fd400d20c5fd5ec9a23e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272869} {:answer/id #uuid "421729c9-7121-58d8-860c-796cda7b5c78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/40/402d90507403eabf4cd35cde83a45c9fa2d8080347e1debb0e2463be408b489b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272952} {:answer/id #uuid "9ae601cb-9bca-50d6-915e-fe378f1fcdbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/33/338809ca0a3fe4d02c3523ec5e34a8d07a00b297d9f468740bbd1800d9675941.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "421729c9-7121-58d8-860c-796cda7b5c78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/40/402d90507403eabf4cd35cde83a45c9fa2d8080347e1debb0e2463be408b489b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272952} :answer-field/id #uuid "87e5e43a-9b64-5f59-a8f9-8d8600a7df12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274868}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "59f09d6c-7a4e-5350-aa9e-955b620390c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-158193" :question/problem "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x,y)$ is defined for all points $(x,y)$ on the plane, hence the domain is the entire $xy$-plane. \n\n![](images/40/402d90507403eabf4cd35cde83a45c9fa2d8080347e1debb0e2463be408b489b.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275456 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2af093ec-bae8-5f02-ba64-69ec4eb07e90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/30/3070e936fea02f7c02b2e6bc780534b80108db28836c4c4615954e8063590867.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272766} {:answer/id #uuid "a256b260-fed0-59a9-a2a1-4c844aa7d23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/45/45c170dbe0048816d6490ff39c6144d3ac42298dff9c2fa71cb22217d358ce1a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273792} {:answer/id #uuid "b3c94091-efa3-5941-be60-4cf65defa0fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2d/2ddf4edfd91b14835e7b14ca8cebf08b82b8585d9fd18972c8b065d6153a62f0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273944} {:answer/id #uuid "d9e66f66-040b-5940-b7d6-5c2fb64af2da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f0/f04a668ae876db9e3a26f8ce7cc8bfcaac1149ee221622c22343483fd89